Z||000004||Fiero_24||07-21-2001||01:04 PM||||Cheever, you actually like the short shifter?  I had one and since you lose all that leverage from a longer shifter it makes it a pain to drive (plus it is not faster to shift in my opinion).  The day I sold my Coupe I put the stock shifter back on and it was so much nicer to shift.  Not bashing on them, just saying they are not for everyone.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bluebottlejunky||07-21-2001||01:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Adrift:<BR><B>Bluebottlejunky - Steel gas, break and clutch pedal? Where did you get them from? How much did it cost?<BR>Thanks<BR>ARi</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It was a steel clucth pedal, becuase in the earlier year fiero 84-86 I think had an aluminum pedal that would tend to bend witch would make my car not disnguage(SP) all the way.  I would have to have that pedal to the floor for every shift, now I don't.  It was like $35 from fiero store..pretty easy to install well not for me im 6'1 220lbs..but other than that easy.  If you get one try <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>  and his archives has an "how to"<BR>Mike<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||07-21-2001||02:36 PM||||Cut Cat. Ass-o-meter tells me I gained some upper end power. Not much, but worth the $30 for the resonator. I'm guessing 3-4 horsies?||||reg||6
Z||000007||Formula||07-21-2001||02:46 PM||||I have mine monochrome painted 1998 viper red, aluminum split spoke american racing wheels 15", carbed 3.2 stroker (supposedly dynoed at 270hp@7000rpms, Im not believing it until I drive it though), alpine stereo, sony xplode sub and 400watt amp, custom interior, carpet goes over the center console, grant steering wheel, and a lot of little things<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||07-21-2001||02:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero_24:<BR><B>Cheever, you actually like the short shifter?  I had one and since you lose all that leverage from a longer shifter it makes it a pain to drive (plus it is not faster to shift in my opinion).  The day I sold my Coupe I put the stock shifter back on and it was so much nicer to shift.  Not bashing on them, just saying they are not for everyone.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sounds like you had a bad set of shift cables.<BR>With good cables , moving the shifter is almost effortless. You could probably get away with lubing the cables.||||reg||1
