Z||000033||ferrari_momo||07-24-2001||11:23 PM||||hmmm....<BR>88 fiero = 3.4 engine, 8.8 MM wires, K&N filter, short shifter with MOMO shift knob, blue engine, and some body mods, <BR>85 fiero= v8, ferrari 308 rebody, MOMO accessories, new interior work, man... lots of things.  too much time and money into these babies.<BR> check out my temporary site. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24/ferrari_momo.html?992954137951" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24/ferrari_momo.html?992954137951</A> <BR>thanks for letting me share  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <BR>pat kalsmith.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000034||mrfiero||07-24-2001||11:44 PM||||I have done a lot to my '88 GT T-Top, but there is still a lot more to do.  <P>I am in the middle of a complete suspension rebuild.  Here's what I'm doing:<P>-1" lowered springs<BR>-new rubber front control arm bushings <BR>-new inner tie rods<BR>-new outer tie rods<BR>-new rack bushing<BR>-poly rear bushings<BR>-new shocks & struts<BR>-new upper & lower ball joints<P>I also have the done the following:<P>-Borla exhaust<BR>-ported manifolds (Jet-Hot coated)<P><BR>Here are some things I've done, but not really considered mods:<P>-new shifter & select cables<BR>-new fuel pump<BR>-new fuel pressure regulator<BR>-new fuel injectors<BR>-newer interior (orig. was shot)<BR>-new subwoofer speaker<BR>-new interior switches<BR>-rebuilt headlight motors<BR>-Rodney's low temp fan switch <BR>-Rodney's select arm rebuild kit<BR>-new front & rear brakes (calipers & rotors)<P><BR>I have a set of real Mecham 3-port side scoops (urethane, not fiberlass) that will go on it soon along with a Mustang scoop for the decklid.  I'll probably put some Trans-Am or Sunbird type grilles on the hood too.<P>I will be installing a newer tranny and Centerforce clutch within the next few weeks too.<P>It will eventually get a built 3.4 with a turbo, but that's down the road.<P>  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000035||87GTBro||07-24-2001||11:57 PM||||I installed a subwoofer enclosure behind the passenger seat similar to the one fierosound did...  Its powered by a 240W amp and active crossover behind the driver's seat and a Kenwood KDC-MP8017 head unit.  (Plays MP3's)<P>I fit 175 full length high quality songs on one CD!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firewallsub.jpg"> ||||reg||1
